<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maharashtra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maharashtra is a state of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, created in 1960 from the Marathi-speaking parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Mumbai</a> as its capital. Its territory includes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a> and much of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-plateau">Deccan plateau</a>. The region was ruled in turn by the Satavahanas, Rashtrakutas, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seuna-yadava-dynasty">Yadavas of Devagiri</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>, and it is the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marathi">Marathi</a> language.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maharashtra.jpg" alt="Maharashtra" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jawahar Soneji · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gateway_of_India_-Mumbai.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Satavahanas rose in the northern Deccan, in what is now <b>Maharashtra</b>, after the Maurya Empire withdrew from the region in the second century BCE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/satavahana-dynasty">Satavahana dynasty · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In <b>Maharashtra</b> Dnyaneshwar completed the Dnyaneshwari, his Marathi commentary on the Bhagavad Gita, in 1290; Namdev and his companions sang of the god Vithoba of Pandharpur, the focus of the Varkari tradition, which Eknath carried on in the 16th century and Tukaram, who died about 1650, in the…</blockquote><a href="/movement/bhakti-movement">Bhakti movement · Course of Events</a></li><li><blockquote>A more radical group, led by Bal Gangadhar Tilak in <b>Maharashtra</b>, Bipin Chandra Pal in Bengal and Lala Lajpat Rai in the Punjab, demanded swaraj, self-rule, and urged swadeshi, the use of Indian goods, together with the boycott of British ones and national education; Tilak’s declaration that swaraj…</blockquote><a href="/movement/indian-independence-movement">Indian independence movement · Aims</a></li><li><blockquote>As the Satavahana dynasty weakened in the early 3rd century, an Abhira chief, Ishvarasena, established a kingdom around Nashik in <b>Maharashtra</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/abhira-dynasty">Abhira dynasty</a></li><li><blockquote>Akkalkot merged into Bombay Province in 1948 and became part of <b>Maharashtra</b> in 1960, in Solapur district.</blockquote><a href="/state/akalkot-state">Akalkot State</a></li><li><blockquote>Aundh merged into Bombay Province in 1948 and became part of <b>Maharashtra</b> in 1960, in Satara district.</blockquote><a href="/state/aundh-state">Aundh State</a></li></ul></section>
